    {"slug":"best-betting-site-odds-ireland","title":"Best Odds Betting Site in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed betting sites in Ireland for odds — lowest overround, best prices on football, racing and major markets for Irish punters.","topic":"odds and value","h2s":["How to Compare Betting Odds","Overround and Margin Explained","Where to Find the Best Odds in Ireland","Why Odds Quality Matters Over Time"],"faqs":[("What is a bookmaker's overround?","The overround is the total implied probability across all outcomes in a market. A 105% overround means the bookmaker has a 5% mathematical edge."),("How do I compare odds across GRAI-licensed sites?","Use an odds comparison tool or check the same market on two or three sites before placing. Even small differences compound over many bets."),("What is a price guarantee?","Some GRAI-licensed bookmakers guarantee the best available price on certain markets — if another licensed site offers better odds at the same time, they match it."),("Does best odds guaranteed apply to all sports?","BOG (best odds guaranteed) is primarily associated with horse racing in Ireland; other sports rarely carry an equivalent guarantee.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-live-streaming-ireland","title":"Best Live Streaming Betting Site in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed betting sites in Ireland for live streaming — watch horse racing, football and tennis free with an account.","topic":"live streaming","h2s":["Live Streaming on Betting Sites in Ireland","Sports Covered by Streaming","How to Access Live Streaming","Best GRAI-Licensed Sites for Streaming"],"faqs":[("Do GRAI-licensed bookmakers offer free live streaming?","Yes. Most major GRAI-licensed bookmakers offer free streaming with an active account balance or recent bet placed."),("What sports can I stream on GRAI-licensed sites?","Horse racing (Irish and UK), football, tennis, greyhounds, cricket and darts are commonly streamed by GRAI-licensed bookmakers."),("Do I need to place a bet to watch streams?","Most GRAI-licensed bookmakers require an active account balance or a qualifying bet placed on the event to access free streaming."),("Can I watch Premier League games on a betting site?","Premier League live rights are held by Sky and TNT Sports in Ireland; most betting sites cannot stream Premier League matches.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-mobile-ireland","title":"Best Mobile Betting Site in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed mobile betting sites in Ireland — fast apps, full market access and mobile-first features for Irish punters on the go.","topic":"mobile betting","h2s":["What Makes a Great Mobile Betting Site?","App vs Mobile Browser Betting","Mobile-Specific Features to Look For","Best GRAI-Licensed Sites for Mobile Betting"],"faqs":[("Is mobile betting legal in Ireland?","Yes. Mobile betting on GRAI-licensed sites is fully legal and accounts for the majority of betting volume in Ireland."),("Do GRAI-licensed bookmakers have apps?","Most major GRAI-licensed bookmakers have dedicated iOS and Android apps; some also have fully optimised mobile browsers."),("What mobile-specific features should I look for?","Fast biometric login, quick-deposit, in-play notifications, mobile cash out and Touch ID/Face ID are features to look for."),("Is mobile betting safe?","On GRAI-licensed sites, yes. GRAI licensing requires security standards including encrypted transactions and secure account verification.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-ios-app-ireland","title":"Best iOS Betting App in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed iOS betting apps in Ireland — iPhone and iPad apps reviewed for speed, features and market access for Irish punters.","topic":"iOS betting apps","h2s":["What to Look for in an iOS Betting App","App Store Availability and Installation","iOS-Specific Features and Biometrics","Best GRAI-Licensed iOS Apps in Ireland"],"faqs":[("Can I download a betting app on my iPhone in Ireland?","Yes. Most major GRAI-licensed bookmakers have iOS apps available from the App Store, free to download."),("Do iOS betting apps support Face ID and Touch ID?","Yes. Most GRAI-licensed bookmakers' iOS apps support biometric login via Face ID and Touch ID for fast, secure access."),("Is Apple Pay available for deposits on iOS betting apps?","Yes. Many GRAI-licensed bookmakers accept Apple Pay deposits directly through their iOS apps."),("Are iOS betting apps the same as the desktop site?","Core functionality is the same, though the app interface is optimised for touch. Some features like live streaming may differ.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-android-app-ireland","title":"Best Android Betting App in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed Android betting apps in Ireland — Google Play and direct download apps reviewed for speed and features.","topic":"Android betting apps","h2s":["Android Betting Apps in Ireland Explained","Google Play and Direct Download Options","Android-Specific Features","Best GRAI-Licensed Android Apps in Ireland"],"faqs":[("Can I download a betting app on my Android phone in Ireland?","Yes. Most GRAI-licensed bookmakers offer Android apps, either via Google Play or as a direct APK download from their website."),("Why are some betting apps not on Google Play?","Google Play has historically restricted some gambling apps in certain regions. Many GRAI-licensed bookmakers offer a direct APK download as an alternative."),("Is Google Pay available on Android betting apps?","Yes. Several GRAI-licensed bookmakers accept Google Pay deposits through their Android apps."),("Do Android betting apps support fingerprint login?","Yes. Most GRAI-licensed bookmakers' Android apps support fingerprint authentication for fast, secure login.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-fast-payout-ireland","title":"Best Fast Payout Betting Site in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed fast payout betting sites in Ireland — same-day withdrawals, Revolut, debit card and e-wallet payout times compared.","topic":"fast payouts","h2s":["Why Fast Payouts Matter","Withdrawal Methods and Processing Times","GRAI Licensing and Payout Obligations","Best GRAI-Licensed Sites for Fast Withdrawals"],"faqs":[("What is the fastest withdrawal method in Ireland?","E-wallets and Revolut typically process withdrawals same-day or within a few hours; debit cards take 1–3 business days."),("Do GRAI-licensed bookmakers have to pay out?","Yes. Paying out winnings is a GRAI licence condition — an operator that refuses to pay winnings is in breach of their licence."),("What is the average withdrawal time at GRAI-licensed sites?","Most GRAI-licensed bookmakers process withdrawals within 1–3 business days; some e-wallet routes are same-day or overnight."),("Are there withdrawal limits at GRAI-licensed bookmakers?","Yes. Most bookmakers have daily/weekly/monthly withdrawal limits; high-volume players should check these before choosing an operator.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-revolut-ireland","title":"Best Betting Site for Revolut in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed betting sites for Revolut in Ireland — instant deposits, fast withdrawals and Revolut compatibility compared.","topic":"Revolut payments","h2s":["Revolut Betting in Ireland: How It Works","Revolut Deposits at GRAI-Licensed Sites","Revolut Withdrawals and Processing Times","Best GRAI-Licensed Sites for Revolut Users"],"faqs":[("Is Revolut accepted at GRAI-licensed betting sites?","Yes. Revolut is widely accepted for deposits and withdrawals at most GRAI-licensed bookmakers operating in Ireland."),("Is Revolut classed as a credit card for betting purposes?","No. Revolut is a prepaid/e-money account and is not subject to the GRAI's credit card ban on gambling deposits."),("How fast are Revolut deposits on betting sites?","Revolut deposits are typically instant, appearing in your betting account immediately."),("How long do Revolut betting withdrawals take?","Withdrawal to Revolut typically takes 1–2 business days at most GRAI-licensed bookmakers.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-apple-pay-ireland","title":"Best Betting Site for Apple Pay in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed betting sites for Apple Pay in Ireland — instant deposits and seamless payments via iPhone and Mac for Irish punters.","topic":"Apple Pay","h2s":["Apple Pay on Betting Sites: How It Works","Deposits With Apple Pay in Ireland","Apple Pay Withdrawals at Betting Sites","Best GRAI-Licensed Sites for Apple Pay"],"faqs":[("Can I use Apple Pay to deposit at a betting site in Ireland?","Yes. Many GRAI-licensed bookmakers accept Apple Pay deposits, available on iPhone, iPad and Mac with Face ID or Touch ID."),("Is Apple Pay classed as a credit card for gambling?","No. Apple Pay is a payment method, not a card type — whether it is accepted depends on the underlying card linked. Debit cards via Apple Pay are accepted; credit cards are not."),("Are Apple Pay withdrawals available at GRAI-licensed bookmakers?","Withdrawals via Apple Pay are less common than deposits. Most GRAI-licensed sites withdraw to your debit card or bank account."),("Is Apple Pay safe for betting?","Apple Pay uses tokenisation — your real card number is never shared with the bookmaker, adding a layer of security to betting deposits.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-google-pay-ireland","title":"Best Betting Site for Google Pay in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed betting sites for Google Pay in Ireland — fast Android deposits and seamless payments for Irish punters.","topic":"Google Pay","h2s":["Google Pay on Betting Sites in Ireland","Depositing with Google Pay","Google Pay vs Other Payment Methods","Best GRAI-Licensed Sites for Google Pay"],"faqs":[("Can I use Google Pay to deposit at a betting site in Ireland?","Yes. Several GRAI-licensed bookmakers accept Google Pay deposits on Android devices."),("Is Google Pay classed as a credit card for gambling?","No. Google Pay is a digital wallet — it uses the underlying payment method (debit card, Revolut etc.). Credit cards are not accepted for gambling deposits under GRAI rules."),("How fast are Google Pay betting deposits?","Google Pay deposits at GRAI-licensed bookmakers are typically instant."),("Are Google Pay withdrawals available?","Most GRAI-licensed bookmakers do not support Google Pay withdrawals; funds are returned to the linked bank or card instead.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-low-minimum-deposit-ireland","title":"Best Low Minimum Deposit Betting Site in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed betting sites in Ireland with low minimum deposits — start betting with €5 or less and compare minimum deposit requirements.","topic":"low minimum deposit","h2s":["Why Minimum Deposits Matter","Low Deposit Betting Sites in Ireland","€5 Minimum Deposit Betting Explained","Best GRAI-Licensed Sites for Casual Punters"],"faqs":[("What is the typical minimum deposit at GRAI-licensed bookmakers?","Most GRAI-licensed bookmakers accept deposits from €5–€10, making online betting accessible for casual punters."),("Can I claim a welcome bonus with a low deposit?","Some welcome offers require a minimum qualifying deposit — typically €10–€20 — to trigger the offer."),("Are low-stake bets available on GRAI-licensed sites?","Yes. Minimum bet sizes are typically €0.10–€1 on most GRAI-licensed bookmakers, so low-deposit players can still access many markets."),("What payment methods work for low deposits?","Revolut, debit card and Apple Pay all support low deposits (from €5+) at most GRAI-licensed betting sites.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-high-stakes-ireland","title":"Best High Stakes Betting Site in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed high stakes betting sites in Ireland — maximum bet limits, VIP programmes and high-volume account policies compared.","topic":"high stakes betting","h2s":["High Stakes Betting in Ireland: What to Know","Maximum Bet Limits at GRAI-Licensed Sites","Account Restrictions and High Rollers","Best GRAI-Licensed Sites for High-Stakes Punters"],"faqs":[("Do GRAI-licensed bookmakers have maximum bet limits?","Yes. All bookmakers have maximum stake limits, which vary by sport, market and event. High-stakes players should check limits before betting."),("Can a bookmaker restrict my account for winning too much?","Yes. Bookmakers can limit stakes on individual accounts, though GRAI licensing provides a formal complaints route if you believe restrictions are unfair."),("What is a VIP programme at a betting site?","VIP or loyalty programmes reward high-volume bettors with account benefits, higher limits, personal account managers and exclusive promotions."),("Is there a GRAI rule on maximum payouts?","GRAI licensing does not impose a universal maximum payout rule — each operator sets their own limits, which must be clearly disclosed.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-each-way-betting-ireland","title":"Best Each-Way Betting Site in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed each-way betting sites in Ireland — place terms, number of places and each-way value for horse racing and golf.","topic":"each-way betting","h2s":["Each-Way Betting Explained","Place Terms and Fraction of Odds","Each-Way Value in Horse Racing and Golf","How to Find the Best Each-Way Betting Site"],"faqs":[("What is each-way betting?","An each-way bet has two parts: a win bet and a place bet. If your selection wins, both parts pay; if it places (but doesn't win), only the place part pays at a fraction of the win odds."),("What are typical place terms in horse racing?","Races with 5–7 runners typically pay 3 places; with 8+ runners, 4 places; with 16+ runners in handicaps, some bookmakers pay 5 places."),("How does the place fraction work?","Common fractions are 1/4 and 1/5 of the win odds. If a horse is 10/1 and the place fraction is 1/4, the place part pays 2.5/1."),("Is each-way betting available on golf at GRAI-licensed sites?","Yes. Each-way golf betting typically pays 5 places at majors and 4–6 places at regular tour events at most GRAI-licensed bookmakers.")]},

    # User-type specific (20)
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-beginners-ireland","title":"Best Betting Site for Beginners in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed betting sites for beginners in Ireland — easy sign-up, simple markets and responsible gambling tools explained.","topic":"beginner bettors","h2s":["Getting Started With Betting in Ireland","Choosing Simple Markets as a Beginner","Understanding Odds Formats","Responsible Gambling Tools for New Bettors"],"faqs":[("What is the easiest betting market for beginners?","Match winner (1X2 for football) or win/place in horse racing are the simplest starting points with clear outcomes."),("How do I open an account with a GRAI-licensed bookmaker?","Visit the site, click 'Register', provide ID details, complete age verification and make your first deposit via debit card or Revolut."),("What do betting odds mean?","Odds show how much you win relative to your stake. Odds of 3/1 (or 4.00 decimal) mean you win €3 for every €1 staked; odds-on (e.g. 1/2) mean you must stake €2 to win €1."),("What responsible gambling tools should I use as a beginner?","Set a deposit limit on your account before you bet. GRAI-licensed bookmakers are legally required to offer these tools — use them from the start.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-matched-betting-ireland","title":"Best Betting Site for Matched Betting in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed betting sites for matched betting in Ireland — free bet offers, back/lay market availability and offer frequency compared.","topic":"matched betting","h2s":["Matched Betting in Ireland Explained","How Matched Betting Works With Free Bets","Exchange Access and Lay Betting","Best GRAI-Licensed Sites for Matched Bettors"],"faqs":[("Is matched betting legal in Ireland?","Yes. Matched betting is a legal technique using bookmaker free bets. The technique itself is not illegal, though bookmakers may limit accounts."),("Do I need a betting exchange for matched betting?","Yes. Matched betting typically requires a betting exchange (to lay bets) alongside a bookmaker (to back bets), locking in guaranteed profit from free bets."),("Which GRAI-licensed sites have the most matched betting offers?","Look for bookmakers with frequent free bet promotions, reload bonuses and acca insurance, as these generate the most matched betting opportunities."),("Can bookmakers close my account for matched betting?","Bookmakers can restrict or close accounts. Matched bettors should spread activity across multiple GRAI-licensed sites.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-value-betting-ireland","title":"Best Betting Site for Value Betting in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed value betting sites in Ireland — sharp odds, high limits and account longevity for Irish value bettors.","topic":"value betting","h2s":["What Is Value Betting?","Finding Value Odds at GRAI-Licensed Sites","Keeping Accounts Open as a Value Bettor","Best Sites for Long-Term Value Betting"],"faqs":[("What is a value bet?","A value bet is one where the true probability of an outcome is higher than the implied probability in the bookmaker's odds — meaning the price is better than it should be."),("How do I find value bets?","Compare your own probability estimate to the implied probability in the odds. If you assess a team at 60% chance of winning and the odds imply 50%, there is value."),("Do GRAI-licensed bookmakers restrict value bettors?","Bookmakers can limit accounts they identify as winning bettors. Using multiple GRAI-licensed sites reduces this risk."),("What tools help identify value bets?","Odds comparison sites, expected goals (xG) models for football, and form databases are all tools value bettors use to find mispriced odds.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-ante-post-ireland","title":"Best Ante-Post Betting Site in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed ante-post betting sites in Ireland — Cheltenham futures, Grand National ante-post and horse racing ante-post terms.","topic":"ante-post betting","h2s":["Ante-Post Betting Explained","Cheltenham and Grand National Ante-Post","Ante-Post Terms and Non-Runner Policies","How to Find the Best Ante-Post Value"],"faqs":[("What is ante-post betting?","Ante-post betting means placing bets on an event well in advance — often weeks or months before it takes place — usually at fixed odds."),("What happens to an ante-post bet if my selection doesn't run?","Unless the bookmaker offers 'non-runner no bet' (NRNB) on that market, your stake is lost if the horse is withdrawn."),("Is ante-post betting good value?","It can be — longer-range ante-post markets often carry more value than day-of-event odds, especially for major festivals like Cheltenham."),("Do GRAI-licensed sites offer non-runner no bet on ante-post markets?","Some do, particularly on featured race ante-post markets. Always check the terms before placing.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-in-running-ireland","title":"Best In-Running Betting Site in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed in-running betting sites in Ireland — fastest odds, in-play suspension times and in-running horse racing markets.","topic":"in-running betting","h2s":["In-Running Betting: How It Works","Speed and Reliability in In-Running Markets","In-Running Horse Racing and Football","Best GRAI-Licensed Sites for In-Running Bettors"],"faqs":[("What is in-running (in-play) betting?","In-running betting means placing bets after an event has started, with odds updating in real time based on what is happening."),("How fast do in-running odds update?","The best GRAI-licensed sites update in-running odds within seconds; look for sites with minimal suspension time between odds changes."),("Is in-running horse racing betting available in Ireland?","Yes. In-running racing markets are available on most GRAI-licensed bookmakers, with live video feeds on some sites."),("Can I cash out in-running bets?","Yes. Cash out is typically available on in-running bets on most GRAI-licensed bookmakers, subject to market availability.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-multiple-bets-ireland","title":"Best Betting Site for Multiple Bets in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed betting sites in Ireland for multiple bets — accas, doubles, trebles, Lucky 15s and system bets compared.","topic":"multiple bets","h2s":["Multiple Bets: Doubles, Trebles and Beyond","Accumulators and System Bets Explained","Multiple Bet Promotions in Ireland","Best GRAI-Licensed Sites for Multiple Bet Punters"],"faqs":[("What is the difference between a double and a treble?","A double combines two selections — both must win for the bet to pay. A treble does the same with three selections."),("What is a Lucky 15?","A Lucky 15 covers four selections in 15 bets (4 singles, 6 doubles, 4 trebles, 1 four-fold accumulator), guaranteeing a return if one selection wins."),("What are system bets?","System bets (like Trixie, Patent, Yankee) cover multiple combinations from your selections, paying out even if not all legs win."),("Do GRAI-licensed sites offer acca bonuses on multiple bets?","Yes. Many GRAI-licensed bookmakers offer percentage bonuses on winning accumulators, increasing as the number of legs increases.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-singles-ireland","title":"Best Betting Site for Singles in Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed betting sites in Ireland for single bets — lowest margins, highest limits and best odds for single-bet punters.","topic":"single bet strategies","h2s":["Why Singles Are the Foundation of Betting","Finding the Best Odds for Singles","Maximum Stakes and Single Bet Limits","Best GRAI-Licensed Sites for Single Bettors"],"faqs":[("What is a single bet?","A single bet is a wager on one outcome only — it wins or loses on that one selection, with no accumulator element."),("Are singles or accas better value?","Singles at the best available price are usually better expected value, as each accumulator leg multiplies the bookmaker's margin."),("Do GRAI-licensed bookmakers impose lower limits on singles?","Maximum single-bet limits vary by sport and market; some bookmakers impose lower limits on punters with strong winning records."),("How do I find the best single-bet odds in Ireland?","Use odds comparison tools and check two or three GRAI-licensed bookmakers before placing — even a small price difference adds up over time.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-new-accounts-2026-ireland","title":"Best New Account Offers at Irish Betting Sites 2026","desc":"Best new account welcome offers at GRAI-licensed betting sites in Ireland — free bets, matched deposits and risk-free bets compared.","topic":"new account offers","h2s":["New Account Offers in Ireland: What's Available?","How to Claim a New Betting Site Offer","Reading the Terms on New Account Bonuses","Best GRAI-Licensed Welcome Offers for 2026"],"faqs":[("What new account offers are available at GRAI-licensed bookmakers?","Matched free bets, deposit bonuses and risk-free first bets are the most common new account offers in Ireland."),("How long do I have to use a new account welcome offer?","Most GRAI-licensed bookmakers give 7–30 days to place qualifying bets and 7–14 days to use credited free bets."),("Can I claim new account offers on mobile?","Yes. All GRAI-licensed bookmaker apps offer the same new account bonuses as the desktop version."),("Is there a minimum deposit required to trigger a welcome offer?","Most welcome offers require a minimum deposit, typically €10–€20, to trigger the free bet or bonus.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-existing-customers-ireland","title":"Best Betting Sites for Existing Customers Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed betting sites for existing customer promotions in Ireland — reload bonuses, acca insurance and ongoing offers compared.","topic":"existing customer promotions","h2s":["Why Existing Customer Offers Matter","Types of Reload and Ongoing Promotions","Acca Insurance and Price Boosts","Best GRAI-Licensed Sites for Regular Punters"],"faqs":[("What ongoing promotions do GRAI-licensed bookmakers offer existing customers?","Reload bonuses, acca insurance, weekly free bets, price boosts and loyalty points are common existing customer promotions."),("Are existing customer offers as good as welcome offers?","Generally not — welcome offers tend to be larger. However, frequent reload offers can add significant value over time."),("Do I need to opt in to existing customer promotions?","Most require you to opt in via the promotions page or app before the qualifying event. Check each offer's terms carefully."),("What is a reload bonus in betting?","A reload bonus gives existing customers a free bet or bonus after making a further deposit, usually tied to a minimum deposit amount.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-recreational-bettors-ireland","title":"Best Betting Site for Recreational Bettors Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed betting sites for recreational punters in Ireland — fun, low-pressure, great experience and responsible gambling tools.","topic":"recreational betting","h2s":["Recreational Betting in Ireland: What to Look For","Making Betting Fun and Sustainable","Responsible Gambling Features for Casual Punters","Best GRAI-Licensed Sites for Recreational Use"],"faqs":[("What makes a betting site good for recreational punters?","An easy-to-use interface, interesting features (bet builder, live streaming), regular small offers and clear responsible gambling tools."),("How much should a recreational bettor deposit?","Only what you can afford to lose for entertainment purposes. GRAI-licensed bookmakers are required to offer deposit limits — set one before you start."),("Are recreational bettors more likely to keep their accounts open?","Yes. Bookmakers are less likely to restrict recreational bettors who place normal-size, varied bets rather than high-volume, optimised wagering."),("What responsible gambling features should recreational bettors use?","Deposit limits, session time reminders and reality check prompts are all available on GRAI-licensed bookmakers and worth using.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-professional-bettors-ireland","title":"Best Betting Site for Professional Bettors Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed betting sites for professional punters in Ireland — high limits, sharp odds, account longevity and complaints process.","topic":"professional betting","h2s":["Professional Betting in Ireland: The Landscape","Account Longevity and Bookmaker Relationships","Finding Sharp Prices as a Professional","GRAI Protections for Professional Bettors"],"faqs":[("Can I be refused service by a GRAI-licensed bookmaker?","Yes. Bookmakers can restrict or close accounts at their discretion, though GRAI licensing provides a formal complaints route."),("What recourse does a professional bettor have if restricted?","File a formal complaint with the bookmaker first; if unresolved, escalate to the GRAI, which has jurisdiction over licensed operators."),("Which sports offer the most opportunity for professional bettors?","Horse racing and football tend to have the most market liquidity; niche sports with thinner markets can offer mispriced odds."),("Is professional gambling income taxed in Ireland?","Casual winnings are tax-free; if betting is your primary income and you operate it as a business, Revenue may treat it as taxable. Seek independent tax advice.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-tourists-ireland","title":"Best Betting Site for Tourists Visiting Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed betting sites for tourists in Ireland — easy sign-up, Revolut compatibility and Irish sports coverage for visiting punters.","topic":"tourists visiting Ireland","h2s":["Can Tourists Bet Online in Ireland?","Opening an Account as a Visitor","Irish Sports Worth Betting On","Payment Methods for Tourists in Ireland"],"faqs":[("Can a tourist from the EU bet online in Ireland?","Yes. GRAI-licensed bookmakers accept customers from Ireland, including tourists present in the country."),("Can I use my European bank card to deposit?","Yes. Most GRAI-licensed bookmakers accept European Visa/Mastercard debit cards for deposits."),("What Irish sports should a tourist bet on?","Horse racing (Leopardstown, Navan, Fairyhouse), GAA and rugby — especially if you are visiting during a festival or match week."),("Do I need to verify my identity as a tourist?","Yes. All GRAI-licensed bookmakers require age and identity verification before allowing withdrawals.")]},
    {"slug":"best-betting-site-responsible-gambling-ireland","title":"Best Betting Site for Responsible Gambling Tools Ireland 2026","desc":"Best GRAI-licensed betting sites in Ireland for responsible gambling tools — deposit limits, self-exclusion, reality checks and support links.","topic":"responsible gambling tools","h2s":["Responsible Gambling Features at GRAI-Licensed Sites","Deposit Limits and Spending Controls","Self-Exclusion in Ireland","Getting Help With Problem Gambling"],"faqs":[("What responsible gambling tools are legally required under GRAI?","GRAI-licensed bookmakers must offer deposit limits (daily, weekly, monthly), self-exclusion and referral to gambling support services."),("How do I self-exclude from all GRAI-licensed bookmakers?","Ireland's national self-exclusion register (being rolled out by the GRAI) will allow self-exclusion across all licensed operators. For now, self-exclude individually with each bookmaker."),("What is Gambling Awareness Trust (GAT)?","GAT is Ireland's main problem gambling support service. Freephone 1800 753 753 or visit gamblingcare.ie for free, confidential support."),("How quickly do deposit limits take effect under GRAI rules?","Reductions to deposit limits must take effect immediately on GRAI-licensed bookmakers. Increases require a 24–48 hour delay as a consumer protection measure.")]},
